      "instructions": "You will hear a conversation between a customer and a booking clerk. Answer questions 1-10.",
      "listening_script": "Clerk: Good morning, Riverside Community Centre, how can I help you? Caller: Hi, I'd like to book the main hall for a birthday party. Clerk: Sure, what date were you thinking of? Caller: The twenty-second of March, a Saturday. Clerk: Let me check... yes, that's available. Would that be the morning or evening slot? Caller: Evening, please, from six until eleven. Clerk: Great, and how many guests are you expecting? Caller: Around eighty people. Clerk: Okay, the main hall holds up to one hundred twenty, so that's fine. Can I take your name? Caller: Yes, it's Daniela Kovac, that's K-O-V-A-C. Clerk: And a contact phone number? Caller: 0455 912 384. Clerk: Perfect. Will you need tables and chairs set up? Caller: Yes, please, for eighty people, round tables if possible. Clerk: We can do that. There's a hire fee of two hundred and forty dollars for the hall, plus a refundable deposit of one hundred dollars. Caller: That's fine. Do you also have a sound system available? Clerk: We do, it's an extra thirty-five dollars for the evening. Caller: I'll take that as well then. Clerk: Lovely. I'll send a confirmation email — could I get your email address? Caller: It's daniela dot kovac at mailbox dot com. Clerk: Got it. And finally, is this a private party or should we list it as a public event? Caller: Private, family and friends only. Clerk: All booked in. You'll get the confirmation within the hour.",
