      "instructions": "You will hear a museum guide giving an orientation talk to new visitors. Answer questions 11-20.",
      "listening_script": "Welcome to Bellview Museum, everyone. Before you head off to explore, let me give you a quick overview of the building. We're currently standing in the entrance hall, on the ground floor. To your left is the natural history wing, which houses our dinosaur skeletons and the mineral collection — that's always a favourite with children. To your right is the gift shop and the cafe, which stays open until half an hour after the museum closes. If you go up the stairs behind me, the first floor is entirely dedicated to local history, including a reconstructed nineteenth-century schoolroom you can actually sit in. The second floor holds our temporary exhibitions; this month it's a photography exhibition called 'Coastlines', which runs until the end of next month. Please note that flash photography is not permitted anywhere on the second floor, though it's fine elsewhere in the museum. Restrooms are located on every floor, near the lifts. If you need assistance at any time, our staff wear blue lanyards and are happy to help. Free guided tours leave from this entrance hall on the hour, every hour, and last approximately forty-five minutes. Finally, a reminder that bags larger than a small backpack must be left in the lockers to your right, which are free to use but require a coin deposit that is returned when you collect your bag. Enjoy your visit.",
